    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! The fix has been successfully implemented and tested. Let me provide a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Bug Fixed:** `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `gate` command in the frai CLI uses commander.js to parse arguments. When unknown options like `--ci` are passed, they weren't being included in the `args` array passed to the action handler, even with `.allowUnknownOption(true)` set. This is because `.allowUnknownOption()` only prevents errors\u2014it doesn't automatically pass unknown options through.\n\n**Solution:** Modified the gate command handler in `/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 753-754) to extract the gate arguments directly from `process.argv` instead of relying on commander's parsed `args`. This ensures all flags (both known and unknown) are properly passed through to the frai-gate CLI:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex !== -1 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : args ?? [];\n```\n\n**Testing:** \n- Rebuilt the CLI with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n- Tested in a clean directory: `frai gate init --ci`\n- \u2705 Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created correctly\n\nThe compiled JavaScript has been updated in `packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js` and is ready for deployment.",
